        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "During this hiatus, Percoco accepted payments totaling $35,000 to assist a real-estate development company owned by Steven Aiello in its dealings with Empire State Development, a state agency."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1158",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f3b062f51237430ae3a89ab85890e4cb3002f476cd3ac4f1be40f86822377b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f3b062f5123-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Throughout the proceedings, Percoco argued unsuccessfully that a private citizen cannot commit or conspire to commit honest-services wire fraud based on his own duty of honest services to the public."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1158",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f3b062f51237430ae3a89ab85890e4cb3002f476cd3ac4f1be40f86822377b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f3b062f5123-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "certiorari to the united states court of appeals for the second circuit No. 21\u20131158. Argued November 28, 2022\u2014Decided May 11, 2023"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1158",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f3b062f51237430ae3a89ab85890e4cb3002f476cd3ac4f1be40f86822377b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f3b062f5123-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As noted, Percoco moved before trial for dismissal of the honest-services conspiracy count at issue on the ground that he was out of public offce during part of the time period within the indictment and that a private citizen cannot be convicted of depriving the public of honest services."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1158",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f3b062f51237430ae3a89ab85890e4cb3002f476cd3ac4f1be40f86822377b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f3b062f5123-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We hold that they are not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1158",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f3b062f51237430ae3a89ab85890e4cb3002f476cd3ac4f1be40f86822377b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f3b062f5123-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government does not defend these jury instructions as an accurate statement of the law, but it argues that their imprecision was harmless."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1158",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f3b062f51237430ae3a89ab85890e4cb3002f476cd3ac4f1be40f86822377b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f3b062f5123-0001-0001",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For these reasons, the judgment of the Court of Appeals is reversed, and the case is remanded for further proceedings consistent with this opinion."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
